# Bot1 has Dauthi Voidwalker out on turn 1. On turn 2 Bot2 discards Basking Rootwalla and a Mountain to Faithless
# Looting, and orders the Voidwalker's replacement before madness (CR 616.1): the Rootwalla is exiled with a void counter,
# madness no longer applies (CR 616.1f) and nothing triggers - the stack is empty at the next priority. On turn 3 Bot1
# sacrifices the Voidwalker, chooses the Rootwalla among Bot2's void-countered cards, and casts it for free, which proves
# the void counter is on it: Bot1 controls the Rootwalla. The Voidwalker is Bot1's own card and goes to Bot1's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Dauthi Voidwalker
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Faithless Looting
Basking Rootwalla
Mountain
Mountain x16

